# Line endings, pinned so every clone agrees (copied from methodica-math-ratio-01;
# ADDING-REPORTING-AND-RESUME.md §11.1).
#
# Deployment packages are copied from the WORKING TREE, and this machine runs
# core.autocrlf=true: without eol=lf a package would ship CRLF files that no longer
# match their own commit byte-for-byte (verify-package.ps1 then reports drift).
#
# State when this was added (git ls-files --eol, 2026-09-28): every shipped text file
# is already LF in the index. The only CRLF blobs are ten spec/assets/slide-0NN/
# image10.svg files — generated source material, never shipped — left as they are.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary, so auto-detection is never the only thing between a media file and
# corruption.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary

# SVG is XML — text, not an image format, as far as git is concerned.
*.svg   text eol=lf
